      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that calling `exit()` in the test thread is not the best idea. I took a look at the [mechanics](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/d78952b7ba930e20910c2b6fdac49cc8dc4f709e/subsys/testsuite/ztest/src/ztest.c#L666) of running tests and by calling `exit()`, the test will terminate with `ZTEST_RESULT_PENDING` instead of `ZTEST_RESULT_PASS` which is wrong. We get pass result only because `ret` is initialized with `TC_PASS`.\n\nI think that the test should spawn a new thread. See [test_threads_cancel_abort.c](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/d9eed167d06bae286199cb61c7c9318a6f55ca0d/tests/kernel/threads/thread_apis/src/test_threads_cancel_abort.c) if you need some inspiration.",
