      "message": "digging deeper into the test, I do not believe the test enters `test_panic_data` and we used `k_thread_abort()` function for `_exit`. I printed some logs and I do not see them being printed. I can only see them being printed when I used `abort` instead of `k_thread_abort`. I believe we should give the new thread a `K_ESSENTIAL` for priority. Do you agree?\n\nNow the question is how do I create a new thread in the test. I was looking at your suggestion and I tried the following:\n```\n#include \u003ctests_thread_apis.h\u003e\nk_thread_create(\u0026tdata, tstack, STACK_SIZE, thread_entry_abort,\n\t\t\tNULL, NULL, NULL, K_ESSENTIAL, K_USER, K_NO_WAIT); \n```\n\nHowever, I do not believe the include is correct.\n\nCan you provide some feedback.",
